d his family so  long ago  Zeke's train of thought is something  like this LD ins become Titans Titans  are bad and kill a lot of people people  fear Titans people hate LD ins people  treat LD ends cruelly no one is happy LD  and should cease to exist my major issue  with zis philosophy besides it being a  pessimistic one is that Zeek feels  justified in deciding what's best for  other people just as Grisha unfairly  tried to force Zeek to adopt his  philosophy Zeek is doing the same Grisha  should have recognized seeks  individuality respected his feelings and  given him the freedom to choose his own  path in the same way Zeek should  recognize the individuality of other LD  UNS respect their own feelings and give  them the freedom to choose what they  want who is Zeek to the side that is  merciful to kill an LDN shouldn't that  Aldean be able to decide for him or  herself if they want to live if life has  Worth if the good outweighs the bad for  them I have major issues with the fact  that Zeek forces his own philosophy on  others stripping them of their freedom  to choose  besides why does ich think that the  technological innovations that are  supposed to surpass the power of the  Titans soon won't make life just as bad  as the Titans made it or worse in my  view it is naive to think that getting  rid of LD ins and Titans will solve  everyone else's problems sure they may  live in fear of titans now but even  after the titans are gone they will have  to live in fear of weapons of mass  destruction despite my issues with what  appears to be Zeke's philosophy at this  point I think that ISA yama does a good  job of illustrating how the world is not  black and white everyone is fighting an  attack on titan for what they believe is  good and what that good looks like is  often influenced by their own tragic  backstories in my view Zeke's actions  are completely unjustified nevertheless  Yama does a good job of humanizing the  beast Titan user who seemed like the  in